1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,425
Jeju’s black-rock coast opens onto water so

2
00:00:03,425 --> 00:00:05,740
clear it looks turquoise.

3
00:00:06,618 --> 00:00:08,438
At Sunrise Peak

4
00:00:08,438 --> 00:00:11,798
a volcanic crater rises straight from the sea.

5
00:00:12,132 --> 00:00:13,352
On Udo

6
00:00:13,352 --> 00:00:16,212
quiet coastal roads invite you to slow down

7
00:00:16,212 --> 00:00:17,192
and explore.

8
00:00:17,742 --> 00:00:20,282
And on the south coast

9
00:00:20,282 --> 00:00:23,382
waterfalls tumble into a very different landscape.

10
00:00:25,104 --> 00:00:25,824
By the end

11
00:00:25,824 --> 00:00:28,178
you’ll have the three-day route in order

12
00:00:28,178 --> 00:00:30,723
plus practical options for getting around and

13
00:00:30,723 --> 00:00:31,984
changing weather.

14
00:00:32,562 --> 00:00:35,502
Here is the island at a glance:

15
00:00:35,502 --> 00:00:36,442
west coast

16
00:00:36,442 --> 00:00:37,502
east coast

17
00:00:37,502 --> 00:00:39,482
then the mountain or the south.

18
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:42,524
Three days in Jeju

19
00:00:42,524 --> 00:00:44,144
planned plainly.

20
00:00:45,174 --> 00:00:49,154
A little planning makes this route much easier.

21
00:00:49,154 --> 00:00:51,014
Jeju is bigger than it looks

22
00:00:51,014 --> 00:00:52,694
so think about your transport

23
00:00:52,694 --> 00:00:53,434
your base

24
00:00:53,434 --> 00:00:55,614
and the day’s weather before you set off.

25
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,800
For a short trip

26
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,900
Jeju City is a practical base.

27
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:01,500
It is close to the airport

28
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,540
and many restaurants and buses start there.

29
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:07,000
Aewol on the west or Seogwipo on the south

30
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,680
are alternatives if you want to stay by the coast.

31
00:01:10,242 --> 00:01:12,182
If you plan to rent a car

32
00:01:12,182 --> 00:01:13,982
bring your passport and an International

33
00:01:13,982 --> 00:01:15,122
Driving Permit

34
00:01:15,122 --> 00:01:18,682
or the type of licence Korea accepts from your country.

35
00:01:18,682 --> 00:01:20,642
Check the requirements before you travel.

36
00:01:21,204 --> 00:01:25,844
Book flights from Seoul early for weekends and holidays.

37
00:01:25,844 --> 00:01:27,644
This is one of the busiest air routes in

38
00:01:27,644 --> 00:01:28,644
the world

39
00:01:28,644 --> 00:01:31,264
so leaving flights until the last moment can

40
00:01:31,264 --> 00:01:32,684
make your plans harder.

41
00:01:33,366 --> 00:01:35,866
Jeju weather changes quickly

42
00:01:35,866 --> 00:01:37,686
and wind is common.

43
00:01:37,686 --> 00:01:39,946
Pack a windproof layer whatever the season

44
00:01:39,946 --> 00:01:42,606
and check conditions before outdoor plans

45
00:01:42,606 --> 00:01:45,046
especially a mountain hike or a ferry trip.

46
00:01:45,624 --> 00:01:48,684
Day one follows Jeju’s west coast

47
00:01:48,684 --> 00:01:50,564
with a cafe stop

48
00:01:50,564 --> 00:01:51,264
a beach walk

49
00:01:51,264 --> 00:01:53,784
and an indoor or outdoor afternoon.

50
00:01:54,186 --> 00:01:56,086
Start in Aewol

51
00:01:56,086 --> 00:01:57,866
continue to Hyeopjae

52
00:01:57,866 --> 00:02:00,186
then head inland for the afternoon.

53
00:02:00,636 --> 00:02:05,036
Begin with a coastal drive from Jeju City to Aewol.

54
00:02:05,036 --> 00:02:06,996
Lava rock borders the shoreline

55
00:02:06,996 --> 00:02:09,756
and cafes look out over the water.

56
00:02:09,756 --> 00:02:13,016
Haejigae Cafe is a relaxed place to pause and

57
00:02:13,016 --> 00:02:14,356
enjoy the sea view.

58
00:02:14,694 --> 00:02:15,474
Next

59
00:02:15,474 --> 00:02:18,114
take a slow walk at Hyeopjae Beach.

60
00:02:18,114 --> 00:02:20,454
The water is clear and turquoise

61
00:02:20,454 --> 00:02:23,034
and Biyangdo sits just offshore.

62
00:02:23,034 --> 00:02:23,974
In summer

63
00:02:23,974 --> 00:02:25,494
people come to swim;

64
00:02:25,494 --> 00:02:26,634
in other seasons

65
00:02:26,634 --> 00:02:29,714
the sand and coastal path make a lovely walk.

66
00:02:30,048 --> 00:02:31,168
For lunch

67
00:02:31,168 --> 00:02:32,928
head to nearby Hallim.

68
00:02:32,928 --> 00:02:36,068
Then choose the afternoon around the weather.

69
00:02:36,068 --> 00:02:38,948
Arte Museum Jeju is a large immersive digital

70
00:02:38,948 --> 00:02:42,668
art space and a useful indoor plan when rain

71
00:02:42,668 --> 00:02:45,288
makes a long outdoor stop less appealing.

72
00:02:46,002 --> 00:02:47,742
On a clear day

73
00:02:47,742 --> 00:02:51,442
swap the museum for a short climb up an oreum

74
00:02:51,442 --> 00:02:54,162
one of Jeju’s small volcanic cones.

75
00:02:54,162 --> 00:02:56,442
You get a different view over the fields and

76
00:02:56,442 --> 00:02:59,022
a taste of the island’s volcanic landscape.

77
00:02:59,508 --> 00:03:02,708
Stay on the west coast for sunset.

78
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:05,548
This side of the island faces the evening light

79
00:03:05,548 --> 00:03:07,288
so you can finish the day by the water

80
00:03:07,288 --> 00:03:09,748
before driving back to Jeju City.

81
00:03:11,622 --> 00:03:15,222
Day two is an early start on the east coast

82
00:03:15,222 --> 00:03:16,822
with a crater climb

83
00:03:16,822 --> 00:03:17,782
a ferry to Udo

84
00:03:17,782 --> 00:03:19,822
and a walk above the sea.

85
00:03:20,184 --> 00:03:22,744
The route starts at Seongsan

86
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:23,824
crosses to Udo

87
00:03:23,824 --> 00:03:25,804
then continues to Seopjikoji.

88
00:03:26,442 --> 00:03:29,942
Start early at Seongsan Ilchulbong

89
00:03:29,942 --> 00:03:32,782
also called Sunrise Peak.

90
00:03:32,782 --> 00:03:35,582
This huge volcanic crater rises from the sea

91
00:03:35,582 --> 00:03:39,802
and is part of Jeju’s UNESCO World Natural Heritage.

92
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:42,462
The steps to the crater rim take about twenty

93
00:03:42,462 --> 00:03:43,602
to thirty minutes.

94
00:03:44,244 --> 00:03:47,184
Come for sunrise or early in the morning to

95
00:03:47,184 --> 00:03:49,184
avoid tour groups.

96
00:03:49,184 --> 00:03:50,324
After your visit

97
00:03:50,324 --> 00:03:54,424
go to nearby Seongsan Port for the ferry to Udo.

98
00:03:54,424 --> 00:03:55,824
Check ferry conditions on the day

99
00:03:55,824 --> 00:03:59,724
because bad weather or strong wind can cancel sailings.

100
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:03,123
Udo is a small island with white-sand beaches

101
00:04:03,123 --> 00:04:04,399
quiet coastal roads

102
00:04:04,399 --> 00:04:05,782
and peanut ice cream.

103
00:04:05,782 --> 00:04:07,271
Rent a bicycle, e-bike

104
00:04:07,271 --> 00:04:08,707
or scooter to explore.

105
00:04:08,707 --> 00:04:11,525
Take your time here rather than treating the

106
00:04:11,525 --> 00:04:14,378
island as just another quick photo stop.

107
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:15,607
Back on Jeju

108
00:04:15,607 --> 00:04:17,924
walk the clifftop path at Seopjikoji.

109
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:19,819
It is just south of Seongsan

110
00:04:19,819 --> 00:04:22,610
and the views look back toward Sunrise Peak.

111
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:24,769
On the way back toward Jeju City

112
00:04:24,769 --> 00:04:27,349
families and adventure lovers can consider

113
00:04:27,349 --> 00:04:29,492
Jeju Leports Land in Jocheon.

114
00:04:30,162 --> 00:04:32,462
For your final day

115
00:04:32,462 --> 00:04:34,182
choose one big plan:

116
00:04:34,182 --> 00:04:37,142
a mountain hike or a slower day among the

117
00:04:37,142 --> 00:04:39,062
south coast waterfalls and market.

118
00:04:39,732 --> 00:04:42,018
Hallasan is the mountain option.

119
00:04:42,018 --> 00:04:44,664
The south-coast route links Seogwipo’s

120
00:04:44,664 --> 00:04:47,972
waterfalls with the Olle Trail and market.

121
00:04:48,582 --> 00:04:50,838
Hallasan is Korea’s highest mountain

122
00:04:50,838 --> 00:04:54,039
at one thousand nine hundred and forty-seven metres.

123
00:04:54,039 --> 00:04:55,193
The summit routes

124
00:04:55,193 --> 00:04:56,714
Seongpanak and Gwaneumsa

125
00:04:56,714 --> 00:04:59,338
take most of a day and require an online

126
00:04:59,338 --> 00:05:01,437
reservation for the final section.

127
00:05:01,437 --> 00:05:03,850
Check the official Hallasan website for

128
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:05,042
current rules.

129
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:08,340
If you want a shorter mountain walk

130
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:10,240
try the Eoseungsaengak trail.

131
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,560
It takes about an hour up and down and

132
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,800
gives you a taste of Hallasan without

133
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,400
committing to a summit hike.

134
00:05:17,106 --> 00:05:19,826
For any mountain walk

135
00:05:19,826 --> 00:05:23,066
start early and bring water and warm layers.

136
00:05:23,066 --> 00:05:25,306
Hallasan can be much colder and windier than

137
00:05:25,306 --> 00:05:26,046
the coast

138
00:05:26,046 --> 00:05:29,346
so check the weather before you leave and be

139
00:05:29,346 --> 00:05:30,846
ready to change plans.

140
00:05:31,212 --> 00:05:34,452
If you choose the south instead

141
00:05:34,452 --> 00:05:36,372
cross to Seogwipo.

142
00:05:36,372 --> 00:05:39,432
Jeongbang Falls drops straight into the sea

143
00:05:39,432 --> 00:05:41,592
making it a striking first stop on this

144
00:05:41,592 --> 00:05:42,512
coastal day.

145
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:46,130
Continue to Cheonjiyeon Falls

146
00:05:46,130 --> 00:05:48,370
which is lit in the evening.

147
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:50,850
Then walk a section of the Jeju Olle Trail

148
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:54,610
along the coast before heading into town for a

149
00:05:54,610 --> 00:05:55,350
relaxed finish.

150
00:05:56,208 --> 00:05:59,085
Finish at Seogwipo Maeil Olle Market for

151
00:05:59,085 --> 00:06:01,003
snacks and Jeju tangerines.

152
00:06:01,003 --> 00:06:04,898
If your visit falls on the second or seventh, twelfth

153
00:06:04,898 --> 00:06:06,696
seventeenth, twenty-second

154
00:06:06,696 --> 00:06:08,914
or twenty-seventh of the month

155
00:06:08,914 --> 00:06:11,851
Jeju City’s Traditional Five-Day Market is

156
00:06:11,851 --> 00:06:14,668
another option before you fly home.

157
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:17,566
A car makes this three-day plan much easier

158
00:06:17,566 --> 00:06:19,966
because Jeju’s sights are spread across a

159
00:06:19,966 --> 00:06:21,050
large island.

160
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,653
Most visitors rent a car.

161
00:06:23,653 --> 00:06:26,915
You will need an International Driving Permit

162
00:06:26,915 --> 00:06:30,902
or the kind of licence Korea accepts from your country

163
00:06:30,902 --> 00:06:32,231
and your passport.

164
00:06:32,231 --> 00:06:34,949
Use Naver Map or KakaoMap for driving

165
00:06:34,949 --> 00:06:36,820
directions and routes.

166
00:06:37,182 --> 00:06:40,762
You can also reach every stop by bus

167
00:06:40,762 --> 00:06:43,082
but journeys take much longer.

168
00:06:43,082 --> 00:06:45,222
If you rely on buses

169
00:06:45,222 --> 00:06:49,442
drop one stop per day and check routes before leaving.

170
00:06:49,442 --> 00:06:52,962
Buses may run only every half hour or less often

171
00:06:52,962 --> 00:06:54,962
and timetables can change.

172
00:06:55,392 --> 00:06:56,832
For the east coast

173
00:06:56,832 --> 00:06:59,292
a taxi or day tour can be a useful

174
00:06:59,292 --> 00:07:01,492
alternative to driving.

175
00:07:01,492 --> 00:07:04,252
Keep the day flexible around the Udo ferry

176
00:07:04,252 --> 00:07:07,252
since wind or bad weather can disrupt the crossing.

177
00:07:07,842 --> 00:07:10,562
These are the common ways to make a short

178
00:07:10,562 --> 00:07:12,942
Jeju trip harder than it needs to be.

179
00:07:13,452 --> 00:07:16,312
The main things to watch are trying to fit

180
00:07:16,312 --> 00:07:17,772
in too much

181
00:07:17,772 --> 00:07:20,152
relying on unplanned bus trips

182
00:07:20,152 --> 00:07:22,012
assuming ferries always sail

183
00:07:22,012 --> 00:07:25,172
and treating Hallasan like a warm coastal walk.

184
00:07:25,614 --> 00:07:27,114
First

185
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:30,454
do not plan the whole island in a single day.

186
00:07:30,454 --> 00:07:33,414
This itinerary works because it gives the west, east

187
00:07:33,414 --> 00:07:36,074
and south or mountain their own days.

188
00:07:36,074 --> 00:07:37,914
If you are travelling by bus

189
00:07:37,914 --> 00:07:40,374
cut a stop rather than racing between sights.

190
00:07:40,968 --> 00:07:42,128
Second

191
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:46,008
check your bus route and times before setting off.

192
00:07:46,008 --> 00:07:47,508
Buses reach the main stops

193
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:49,308
but they are slower than driving

194
00:07:49,308 --> 00:07:53,188
and some come only every half hour or less often.

195
00:07:53,188 --> 00:07:54,408
Timetables can change

196
00:07:54,408 --> 00:07:56,388
so check again before each journey.

197
00:07:56,778 --> 00:07:57,231
Third

198
00:07:57,231 --> 00:08:00,008
do not assume the Udo ferry will run in

199
00:08:00,008 --> 00:08:01,538
every kind of weather.

200
00:08:01,538 --> 00:08:04,541
Strong wind or bad conditions can cancel it.

201
00:08:04,541 --> 00:08:05,788
Check on the day

202
00:08:05,788 --> 00:08:08,621
and keep enough flexibility to adjust your

203
00:08:08,621 --> 00:08:09,998
east-coast plan.

204
00:08:11,484 --> 00:08:13,841
And do not underestimate Hallasan.

205
00:08:13,841 --> 00:08:16,729
It is colder and windier than the coast.

206
00:08:16,729 --> 00:08:19,145
Summit routes also have reservation

207
00:08:19,145 --> 00:08:21,974
requirements and strict cut-off times for

208
00:08:21,974 --> 00:08:23,742
starting the final climb

209
00:08:23,742 --> 00:08:26,747
so check the rules and weather rather than

210
00:08:26,747 --> 00:08:28,344
simply showing up.

211
00:08:28,638 --> 00:08:31,578
Is three days enough for Jeju?

212
00:08:31,578 --> 00:08:33,278
It is enough for the west coast

213
00:08:33,278 --> 00:08:34,218
the east coast

214
00:08:34,218 --> 00:08:36,958
and either Hallasan or the south coast.

215
00:08:36,958 --> 00:08:38,778
With four or five days

216
00:08:38,778 --> 00:08:40,638
you can slow down

217
00:08:40,638 --> 00:08:42,138
add beaches and oreum

218
00:08:42,138 --> 00:08:44,858
and keep a spare day for rain or a

219
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:45,458
cancelled ferry.

220
00:08:46,008 --> 00:08:47,432
Do you need a car?

221
00:08:47,432 --> 00:08:49,628
It makes the trip much easier

222
00:08:49,628 --> 00:08:51,408
but it is not essential.

223
00:08:51,408 --> 00:08:53,426
Buses reach the main sights;

224
00:08:53,426 --> 00:08:55,028
just plan fewer stops

225
00:08:55,028 --> 00:08:56,215
allow more time

226
00:08:56,215 --> 00:08:59,301
and check current routes and times on Naver

227
00:08:59,301 --> 00:09:00,788
Map or KakaoMap.

228
00:09:01,122 --> 00:09:04,062
Do you need to book Hallasan?

229
00:09:04,062 --> 00:09:04,802
Yes

230
00:09:04,802 --> 00:09:06,842
for the final summit sections on the

231
00:09:06,842 --> 00:09:10,062
Seongpanak and Gwaneumsa trails.

232
00:09:10,062 --> 00:09:13,122
Shorter trails do not need a reservation.

233
00:09:13,122 --> 00:09:15,722
Check the official Hallasan website because

234
00:09:15,722 --> 00:09:17,322
rules can change.

235
00:09:17,772 --> 00:09:20,272
Keep the plan simple:

236
00:09:20,272 --> 00:09:22,392
spend day one on the west coast

237
00:09:22,392 --> 00:09:24,492
day two around Seongsan and Udo

238
00:09:24,492 --> 00:09:27,772
then choose Hallasan or Seogwipo for day three.

239
00:09:27,772 --> 00:09:28,592
Check weather

240
00:09:28,592 --> 00:09:29,732
ferry conditions, routes

241
00:09:29,732 --> 00:09:31,972
and current rules before setting out.

242
00:09:32,430 --> 00:09:33,500
The full guide

243
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,923
with maps and links for every stop

244
00:09:35,923 --> 00:09:38,233
is free at Korea Plainly dot com.

245
00:09:38,233 --> 00:09:41,163
The link is at the top of the description.

246
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:42,233
If this helped

247
00:09:42,233 --> 00:09:43,923
subscribe for more plain

248
00:09:43,923 --> 00:09:45,970
practical guides to Korea.

